From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] esp32/machine_hw_spi: Raise when a transfer can't be queued.

machine_hw_spi_transfer() ignores what spi_device_queue_trans() returns and
then waits with portMAX_DELAY for the transaction's result. When the queue
call fails, nothing was queued, so that wait never ends and the interpreter
hangs with no error.

It fails when the driver can't allocate a DMA bounce buffer: a buffer in
PSRAM, or one that isn't word-aligned, is copied into internal DMA-capable
RAM, up to 4092 bytes per transaction and two transactions in flight. On a
classic ESP32 with SPIRAM and Classic Bluetooth in a hands-free call, a
display flush from a PSRAM framebuffer hung the interpreter in
spi_device_get_trans_result() in 5 calls of 5, with 3 KB of internal DMA RAM
left, largest block 2.9 KB.

Check the result: on failure collect the transaction still in flight, give
the bus back and raise OSError (ENOMEM for an allocation failure), so the
caller can retry or free memory. Check spi_device_transmit()'s result in the
short-transfer path too.

diff --git a/ports/esp32/machine_hw_spi.c b/ports/esp32/machine_hw_spi.c
index f2b47a0..77e73ca 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/machine_hw_spi.c
+++ b/ports/esp32/machine_hw_spi.c
@@ -343,7 +343,10 @@ static void machine_hw_spi_transfer(mp_obj_base_t *self_in, size_t len, const ui
 
         transaction.flags = SPI_TRANS_USE_TXDATA | SPI_TRANS_USE_RXDATA;
         transaction.length = bits_to_send;
-        spi_device_transmit(self->spi, &transaction);
+        esp_err_t err = spi_device_transmit(self->spi, &transaction);
+        if (err != ESP_OK) {
+            check_esp_err(err);
+        }
 
         if (dest != NULL) {
             memcpy(dest, &transaction.rx_data, len);
@@ -372,7 +375,20 @@ static void machine_hw_spi_transfer(mp_obj_base_t *self_in, size_t len, const ui
                 transaction->rx_buffer = dest + offset;
             }
 
-            spi_device_queue_trans(self->spi, transaction, portMAX_DELAY);
+            esp_err_t err = spi_device_queue_trans(self->spi, transaction, portMAX_DELAY);
+            if (err != ESP_OK) {
+                // Nothing was queued (with a buffer outside DMA-capable RAM, the
+                // driver could not allocate its bounce buffer), so there is no
+                // result to wait for: collect the one in flight, give the bus
+                // back and raise, instead of waiting forever below.
+                if (offset > 0) {
+                    MP_THREAD_GIL_EXIT();
+                    spi_device_get_trans_result(self->spi, &result, portMAX_DELAY);
+                    MP_THREAD_GIL_ENTER();
+                }
+                spi_device_release_bus(self->spi);
+                check_esp_err(err);
+            }
             bits_remaining -= transaction->length;
 
             if (offset > 0) {
